WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
A century ago,

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.640
Australian doctors still treated children for rickets, where

00:00:04.747 --> 00:00:08.080
growing bones soften and bend, and scurvy, where

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.160
gums bleed and wounds won't heal.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.080
Today, the nutrition-linked diseases that fill our hospitals

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.120
are mostly type 2 diabetes and heart disease.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.440
One set comes from too little.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.880
The other is linked to long-term excess, alongside

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.000
other risk factors.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.120
So how does what we eat change disease

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:27.680
risk?

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.780
Earlier, you saw that nutrition is one acquired

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.460
cause of disease.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.420
Here's the chain that explains any case.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.740
Start with the nutrient and its normal job

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.940
in the body.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.500
Then ask what changes when there's too little

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.620
for long enough, a deficiency, or too much

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.340
over many years, an excess.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.060
Then link that change to the effect.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.540
A deficiency takes away a job.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.900
An excess overloads a system that normally works.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:58.980
Take iron.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.940
You've seen its chain already: too little iron

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:05.780
means less haemoglobin, smaller, paler red cells, and

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.420
less oxygen carried, which is iron-deficiency anaemia.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.100
The nutrition question is why the iron is

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:12.660
low.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.980
A diet with too little iron, or a

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.180
gut that absorbs it poorly, makes it a

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.900
nutritional deficiency.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.860
But losing blood, for example from heavy periods

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.740
or bleeding in the gut, drains iron too,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.980
and that cause isn't the diet.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.300
So check where the iron went before you

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.420
call it nutritional.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.833
The same chain works for vitamins.

00:01:34.114 --> 00:01:36.593
Vitamin C is needed by the enzymes that

00:01:36.674 --> 00:01:39.873
build strong collagen, the rope-like protein that holds

00:01:39.954 --> 00:01:42.993
together gums, skin and blood vessel walls.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:46.273
Without it, new collagen is weak, so small

00:01:46.354 --> 00:01:49.953
vessels leak, gums bleed and wounds heal slowly.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.313
That's scurvy.

00:01:52.034 --> 00:01:54.833
Vitamin D lets your gut absorb calcium.

00:01:55.154 --> 00:01:58.273
Without it, growing bones don't harden properly, so

00:01:58.314 --> 00:02:00.113
they can bend under the body's weight.

00:02:00.514 --> 00:02:01.393
That's rickets.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.113
Scurvy has a C in it, for vitamin

00:02:04.274 --> 00:02:04.593
C.

00:02:05.154 --> 00:02:07.233
Rickets, think vitamin D.

00:02:07.714 --> 00:02:09.633
Your skin can make it in sunlight, and

00:02:09.714 --> 00:02:12.033
some foods and supplements supply it too.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:16.873
Iodine adds a twist you'll recognise from homeostasis.

00:02:17.154 --> 00:02:19.793
Your thyroid gland uses iodine to build its

00:02:19.874 --> 00:02:22.433
hormones, which set how fast your cells use

00:02:22.514 --> 00:02:22.993
energy.

00:02:23.474 --> 00:02:26.673
With too little iodine, those hormone levels fall.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:31.873
Negative feedback responds: the pituitary releases more TSH,

00:02:32.034 --> 00:02:36.033
thyroid-stimulating hormone, telling the thyroid to work harder,

00:02:36.074 --> 00:02:37.233
and the gland grows.

00:02:37.794 --> 00:02:40.433
But the missing ingredient is still missing, so

00:02:40.514 --> 00:02:42.593
it keeps enlarging into a goitre.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.473
That's one reason Australian bread has been made

00:02:45.554 --> 00:02:48.273
with iodised salt since 2009.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.460
Now excess, and type 2 diabetes.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.980
Remember what insulin does: it binds to muscle

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:58.780
and fat cells, and that signal moves glucose

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.540
transporters into the membrane, so glucose gets in.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.780
Years of taking in more energy than you

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.220
use, with little activity, build up body fat,

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.100
especially around the liver and other organs.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.500
Muscle and fat cells then respond less to

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.540
insulin.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.380
Insulin still binds, but fewer transporters move, so

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.300
less glucose gets in.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.500
The liver also keeps releasing glucose when insulin

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.100
should slow it down.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.420
Both keep blood glucose high.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.180
That's insulin resistance.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.800
At first, the beta cells in the pancreas

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.680
cover for it by releasing more insulin, so

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.920
blood glucose can stay close to normal for

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:38.560
years.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.600
That's why many people don't know anything's wrong.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.320
Over time, the beta cells may not keep

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.720
up, and blood glucose stays high.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.200
That's type 2 diabetes.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.800
Years of high glucose damage blood vessels, from

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.360
tiny ones in the eyes, kidneys and nerves

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.560
to the arteries feeding the heart.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.360
When the Australian AusDiab study tested adults, about

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.480
half of those with diabetes hadn't been diagnosed.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.180
So does eating too much cause type 2

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.220
diabetes?

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.620
Not on its own.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.420
Compare scurvy: one missing nutrient, and the disease

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:18.020
follows reliably until vitamin C is restored.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.420
Type 2 diabetes is different.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.460
Excess intake is a risk factor, something that

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:27.140
raises the chance of disease without guaranteeing it.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.220
Family history, age, activity, sleep and some medicines

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.540
change the risk too, and so does what

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.180
food people can afford and reach.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.540
Heart disease is similar: saturated fat can raise

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.260
LDL cholesterol, which helps build the plaque you

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.980
saw with smoking, but it's one risk factor

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.020
among several.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.673
Two exam questions.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:49.713
First.

00:04:50.274 --> 00:04:54.113
A fourteen-year-old spends almost all daylight hours indoors.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:57.473
Blood tests show low vitamin D, and their

00:04:57.554 --> 00:04:59.553
gut is absorbing little calcium.

00:05:00.194 --> 00:05:03.473
Using nutrient, change and effect, explain how this

00:05:03.594 --> 00:05:05.873
deficiency could affect their bones.

00:05:06.194 --> 00:05:07.553
Pause here to answer.

00:05:17.967 --> 00:05:20.926
The nutrient is vitamin D, and its job

00:05:21.007 --> 00:05:23.286
is helping the gut absorb calcium.

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:26.366
With little sunlight, the skin makes little vitamin

00:05:26.447 --> 00:05:29.086
D, so less calcium is absorbed.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:32.926
Growing bone doesn't harden properly and stays soft,

00:05:33.007 --> 00:05:35.166
so it can bend under the body's weight,

00:05:35.247 --> 00:05:36.366
which is rickets.

00:05:36.687 --> 00:05:39.726
The classic mistake is answering "drink more milk".

00:05:40.207 --> 00:05:43.806
Without vitamin D, extra calcium isn't absorbed well.

00:05:45.034 --> 00:05:45.593
Second.

00:05:46.074 --> 00:05:48.233
The chart shows new cases of type 2

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:51.673
diabetes per thousand adults each year, in four

00:05:51.754 --> 00:05:54.713
groups sorted by body weight and family history.

00:05:55.274 --> 00:05:57.913
Identify two risk factors the data show.

00:05:58.474 --> 00:06:01.593
Then explain why the claim "eating too much

00:06:01.674 --> 00:06:05.273
causes type 2 diabetes" overstates the evidence.

00:06:05.594 --> 00:06:06.953
Pause here to answer.

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:20.166
Obesity and a family history both go with

00:06:20.327 --> 00:06:22.886
higher rates, and together, the highest.

00:06:23.447 --> 00:06:25.926
But even in the highest group, about thirty

00:06:26.007 --> 00:06:29.046
in a thousand developed diabetes each year, so

00:06:29.207 --> 00:06:32.246
most didn't, and some healthy-weight adults did.

00:06:32.887 --> 00:06:35.286
And the data didn't measure food intake, so

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:37.526
they can't show that eating too much caused

00:06:37.607 --> 00:06:38.646
these cases.

00:06:38.967 --> 00:06:41.446
The classic mistake is treating a higher rate

00:06:41.527 --> 00:06:42.726
as a guarantee.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:47.293
So for any nutrition question, name the nutrient

00:06:47.374 --> 00:06:50.093
and its normal job, say what changes with

00:06:50.174 --> 00:06:52.573
too little or too much, link it to

00:06:52.614 --> 00:06:55.773
the effect, then ask: is this one missing

00:06:55.894 --> 00:06:59.133
nutrient, or one risk factor among many?

00:06:59.694 --> 00:07:02.333
Next, what happens when cell division escapes

00:07:02.894 --> 00:07:05.613
control: how cancer begins and spreads.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:08.273
Here are the key notes.

00:07:08.514 --> 00:07:10.433
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:11.313
to copy them.
